  "rationale": "StatementTyped composes expression typing with binding typing through exactly the intermediate environment shown in Let. SequenceTyped has the empty rule and the cons rule threading the current environment to the same final environment. ProgramTyped is class-table well-formedness plus existence of an empty-input sequence derivation, without a requirement that the final environment be empty. The nil rule's environment-well-formedness premise is the stated environment convention, not an operational premise. unit:given.typing.expressions and unit:given.typing.bindings introduce the component judgments; unit:given.patterns supplies extended statements and the inherited program syntax supplies P, empty and cons. Scope exit/destruction is absent from these definitions, matching the final-storage explanation.",
